    "guidance": "Observed reliability: limited—5/12 (41.7%) in-distribution runs satisfied final red containment. Nine runs first met the containment predicate, but four of those no longer satisfied it at the final state; three never met it. Use is therefore not recommended as the default. Its red-anchored prior is intended for an observed, reachable red whose displacement dominates, but that benefit has no out-of-distribution validation. Avoid when the red pose is stale/noisy/unobservable, the red-to-buffer route is doubtful, contact/phase is ambiguous, or collision/recovery would be required. Recognize failure by lack of red co-motion after closing, red remaining elevated or following the TCP after opening, red outside or later leaving the center, premature blue disturbance, or material/persistent IK residual or limit contact; converged IK alone is not success proof. Handoff to place_blue only after direct observation that red is stationary in the supplied buffer and the gripper/TCP are open and clear; preserve both causal observations. If red is merely displaced but remains visible/reachable, a replan may refresh its anchor. If red is already settled, hand off rather than reacquire; unseen miss/drop/collision states require high-level reassessment."
